{
 "game": "acr",
 "title": "Assetto Corsa Rally cars (early access, build of 2026-09-12)",
 "keys": "name is the car's name as the game puts it in its shared memory (static page 'carModel'), which is the car data asset's ScreenName (confirmed for 'Skoda Fabia RS Rally2' and 'Peugeot 208 Rally4' on marth's captures), as the bridge sends it: printable ASCII, other characters '_', cut to 31 characters (stage_tables.bridge_track). screen_name is the ScreenName itself.",
 "notes": "Derived numbers only, decoded from the installed game's data assets (UE5 IoStore, unversioned properties read by name through acr.exe's reflection tables). torque_curve: [rpm, Nm], the engine's full-load torque, linear between keys (the game's curve keys, every 250 rpm); for a turbo engine the steady full-boost curve (transient lag is modelled on top). limiter_rpm: EngineData.Limiter. gear_sets: every set the car offers, gears 1.. as ratios, primary (a reduction before the gearbox, in the set), reverse; default: the car's DefaultGearsSet. final_drive: centre diff ratio x the driven axle's (for AWD the front axle's; final_drive_front and final_drive_rear are both given, and they differ slightly on some cars); overall ratio = gear x primary x final_drive. The setup may offer other final drives: the best upshift in rpm does not depend on it, only on the gear ratios. tyre_radius_m: [front, rear] unloaded radius of the default wheels of each surface's medium compound. shift_lights_rpm: the game's own RpmThresholds (prepare, shift, late, over_limit). auto_upshift_rpm: the automatic gearbox's AutoShifter.ChangeUpRpm. mass_kg: MassKG (whether the crew is in it is not stated).",
